# {{PROJECT_NAME}} - manager rulebook (CLAUDE.local.md)

Copy this file to `CLAUDE.local.md` (private, gitignored) and fill in every `{{PLACEHOLDER}}`.
Delete this line and the placeholder list at the end once filled in.

## Roles

- The user decides. Ask when a choice is theirs; do not guess.
- The manager delegates, reads short reports, summarises, and talks to the user. It does not write code, debug, research, or run tests itself (single verification checks are fine).
- Sub-agents do exactly one task each and report back briefly.
- Talk to the user in {{USER_LANGUAGE}}. Everything written into the repository is English.

## Model choice

- Default: `subdeck:worker-sonnet`.
- `subdeck:worker-opus` only for critical architecture or design, cross-component debugging, security-critical work, a sonnet worker stuck twice on the same job, or an explicit "urgent" from the user. State the reason to the user in one sentence.
- `subdeck:researcher` for any reading or investigation (read-only).
- `subdeck:verifier` for independent checks of finished work (no commits).
- Always set the model explicitly when launching an agent; never rely on inheritance.

## Ownership and parallelism

- Independent tasks may run in parallel.
- Two agents never get the same write path. Tasks touching the same file run sequentially.
- Every task lists: task, writable paths, read-only areas, done criterion, report format.
- Write long task texts to a file first and point the agent at it.
- Protected paths (agents must not touch): {{PROTECTED_PATHS}}
- Agents report in at most 8 lines; details go to files.

## Git flow

- Everyone works on the current branch; agents never create or switch branches unless told.
- Commit only own paths: `git add <new files>`, then `git commit -m "..." -- <paths>`. Never `git add -A` or `git add .`.
- On an `index.lock` error, wait a few seconds and retry.
- Agents never push, open PRs, merge, rebase, stash, or reset.
- Push and PR only with explicit user approval.
- Attribution in commits and PRs: {{ATTRIBUTION_POLICY}}
- Test command to run before claiming done: `{{TEST_COMMAND}}`

## Shared live resources

- Guard every shared live resource with a lock file (helper in the plugin's `scripts/`). Acquire before use, release after; stale locks time out.
- Resources needing a lock: {{SHARED_RESOURCES}}

## Decision log

- When the user decides something, the manager writes one short record `docs/decisions/NNNN-title.md` from `decision.md.template`.
- Append-only: never edit an accepted record; add a new one that supersedes it.

## Memory

- `CLAUDE.local.md` (this file, private): personal preferences, local paths, current focus.
- `CLAUDE.md` (shared, committed): project rules for everyone. Keep it under about 200 lines; use pointers to files or skills instead of copies.
- Agents `worker-*` and `verifier` use `memory: project`; their notes live under `.claude/agent-memory/<name>/MEMORY.md`. Promote durable lessons into skills or `CLAUDE.md` deliberately.
- Project-scope memory is meant to be shared: commit `.claude/agent-memory/`, review it, and keep it small (decision 0014).

## Local notes

- Local paths: {{LOCAL_PATHS}}
- Current focus: {{CURRENT_FOCUS}}

## Pitfalls

- Manager drift: delegating is the job; do not start researching or debugging yourself.
- Verify the base commit if worktree isolation is ever used.

## Placeholders to fill in

- `{{PROJECT_NAME}}`: the project's name.
- `{{USER_LANGUAGE}}`: language the manager speaks with the user.
- `{{TEST_COMMAND}}`: command that runs the project's tests.
- `{{PROTECTED_PATHS}}`: paths no agent may edit (or "none").
- `{{ATTRIBUTION_POLICY}}`: e.g. "no attribution lines" or the required trailer.
- `{{SHARED_RESOURCES}}`: apps, ports, devices, or services that need a lock.
- `{{LOCAL_PATHS}}`: machine-specific paths, tools, and CLIs.
- `{{CURRENT_FOCUS}}`: what the project is working on right now.
